    "result_text": "The full suite passed (BUILD SUCCESS, the single acceptance test is the only test class; the others are support classes). \n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `capacityWarning` boolean property to the owner response schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec), documenting it as true when the city holds 40\u201349 owners and is approaching the limit of 50.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant alongside the existing `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50`.\n   - Refactored the DTO-stamping helper to keep responsibilities separated: the old `toOwnerDtoWithBulkSignupWarning` became `toOwnerDtoWithWarnings`, which delegates to two focused private methods \u2014 `stampBulkSignupWarning` (unchanged logic) and a new `stampCapacityWarning`. The latter sets `capacityWarning` true when `countOwnersByCity` is in `[40, 50)`, reusing the existing `ClinicService.countOwnersByCity` count.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 (`CityCapacityExceededException`) is untouched. The warning flows through all response paths (create, read, idempotent replay) since they all go through the shared mapping helper.",
